    "result_text": "A held claim now stays in \"claimed\": a hold on either the person or the claim only takes its due figures out of the totals. All 4 tests in `bin/e2e` pass.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Server:** `Person.countsClaimed` (`src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/person/Person.java`) is a new check for whether a claim counts toward claimed. It's the same as the existing `countsLive` check except that holds don't remove the claim. Deferred claims are still left out, and so are open claims of a retired person that no statement has fixed. `Rollup.figures` now uses it for each person's claimed and the claimed-total. It still uses `countsLive` for the due figures (due-total and overdue-total). Claimed and the claimed-total in the ROLLUP and TOTALS audit lines follow from this; the line format is unchanged.\n- **Front end:** a matching `countsClaimed` in `features/claims/useClaims.ts`, plus a new `claimedLive` list in `useSheetFigures.ts`. `PeopleList.tsx` now uses that list for `person-claimed` and `rollup-claimed-total`. Everything else shown still works from the hold-aware `live` list, so the due, overdue, settled/open, aged, tag and month figures behave as before.\n\nNothing about storage changed. Period closing (`PeriodCloser` / `countsAtEnd`) and statements still leave held claims out, since those only work with dues.\n\n**One choice the request didn't settle:** the request only mentions holds, so a retired person's open, unfixed claims still leave claimed as they did before.",
